// datum_units_axis_bare.ri — CLI eval fixture: a BARE axis origin is rejected.
//
// units-length ε (task 5746, R11). `axis_x(point3(0.0, 0.0, 0.0))` passes a
// dimensionless Point3 where a LENGTH triple is required, so `make_axis` returns
// `Value::Undef` and the post-Undef `geometry_diagnose` hook must emit on
// stderr:
//   error: axis_x: ox/oy/oz argument expects Length, got Real; pass a
//   dimensioned length such as `5mm`
// ONE message naming all three coordinates, not one per coordinate: the decoder
// both the gate and the classifier read has ALREADY required the three
// components to share one dimension, so when this fires all three positions
// offend identically and naming them together is COMPLETE information. A bare
// triple is also written as ONE authoring gesture, so one edit-build cycle
// fixes one line.
//
// `reify eval` exits NONZERO: the diagnostic is Severity::Error (C1(iv)).
//
// Lives in tests/fixtures/ (NOT examples/) since it intentionally fails.
//
// Declares its module explicitly, for the same anchor-strength reason as
// datum_units_plane_bare.ri.

module datum_units_axis_bare

structure def DatumUnitsAxisBare {
    let a = axis_x(point3(0.0, 0.0, 0.0))
}
